# One request for every route in docs/SDD.md section 4.1, to send from Visual Studio or Visual Studio Code.
# Start the application first. Under dotnet run it listens on 5080; the container on 8080, so change @host for it.

@host = http://localhost:5080

### The home page: where the application thinks it is running
GET {{host}}/

### Liveness: always 200 and the text "up"
GET {{host}}/healthz/ping

### Readiness: 200 "ready", or 503 "not ready" while starting or stopping
GET {{host}}/healthz/ready

### Fails on purpose: 500 problem details, and an error log line with the exception
GET {{host}}/healthz/error/500

### Refuses on purpose: 403 problem details, and a warning log line
GET {{host}}/healthz/error/403

### Every note, oldest first
GET {{host}}/api/notes

### One note
GET {{host}}/api/notes/1

### Whether a note exists: 200 or 404, no body
HEAD {{host}}/api/notes/1

### The verbs /api/notes answers: 204 with an Allow header
OPTIONS {{host}}/api/notes

### Create a note: 201 with a Location header
POST {{host}}/api/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Created from the .http file.",
  "done": false
}

### Replace a note: both values are required
PUT {{host}}/api/notes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": "Replaced from the .http file.",
  "done": true
}

### Change a note: only the values given
PATCH {{host}}/api/notes/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "done": false
}

### Delete a note: 204, then 404 for a second delete or a GET
DELETE {{host}}/api/notes/2

### An invalid note: 400 problem details naming the field
POST {{host}}/api/notes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "text": ""
}
